# tally 2.1.8 R16, L §4.4 (B5 of group 3's review, agent/t12; p6win, P29): save, a decision whose day is the window
# 03-16 .. 03-25, has fallen by its window's end, so flows over April, after it, is 0.00 PLN: nothing moves there and
# nothing depends on save's day; a span that meets the window (March, 03-20 .. 04-05) stays the window's hole.
# 6a885a9c printed April's two as the hole.
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-06-10
  start 2026-03-01
  end 2026-06-30

source s "s"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
place konto: accounts PLN lives 2026-01-01..
place sav: accounts PLN lives 2026-01-01..
place world: outside lives 1900-01-01..
input keep: money PLN
input d_save: date
input go: bool

move save: transfers
  on d_save
  reads konto
  when go
  leg cash from konto to sav amount max(0 PLN, bal(konto) - keep)

move mm[m in months]: transfers
  on end_of(m) - 1 day
  reads konto
  leg cash from konto to sav amount max(0 PLN, bal(konto) - keep)

version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  keep = 100.00 PLN "s"
  d_save = window(2026-03-16, 2026-03-25) "s"
  go = true "s"
  opening[konto] = 1050.00 PLN at 2026-03-01 start "s"
  opening[sav] = 0.00 PLN at 2026-03-01 start "s"

version st
  cite s
  governs 2026-03..2026-05
  known 2026-01-02
  anchor konto
  stated[konto] = 90.00 PLN after save "saldo"

ask b: bal(konto, 2026-03-31), bal(konto, 2026-04-30), flows(konto, 2026-04), flows(konto, 2026-04-01 .. 2026-04-10), flows(konto, 2026-03), flows(konto, 2026-03-20 .. 2026-04-05)
=== expect
b: (90.00 PLN, 90.00 PLN, 0.00 PLN, 0.00 PLN, ?"date within window(2026-03-16, 2026-03-25) not precise enough for the day of save" (save), ?"date within window(2026-03-16, 2026-03-25) not precise enough for the day of save" (save))
  anchor: konto after save, stated 90.00 PLN, difference ?"date within window(2026-03-16, 2026-03-25) not precise enough for the day of save" (save)
  cut 2026-06-10
warning: WARN-UNREAD place world is read by nothing
